However, oil lamps can be recharged indefinitely with potions of oil.  And,
of course, there's the question of how long you really need to spend in
Gehennom; a brass lantern should last most people fairly well.

(You also forgot to list candles, but they're very weak light sources; most
people never bother with them except for a very specific situation...)

Personally, I've gone through Gehennom with a regular oil lamp; IIRC, I was
most of the way through when it ran out, and didn't bother trying to refill
it.  Went on to ascension.  And that was with a barbarian.  (Just checked my
YAFAP; no light source in my inventory at all.)  My second ascension did
include a magic lamp, but that seemed to be merely a convenience, having
done without it before.  There's really no need for a permanent light source
unless you're doing an extinctionist, imho, and they shouldn't have problems
coming up with a magic lamp.



